# Alpha9 performance configuration (Lighthouse 100%)

Do **not** regress this setup without explicit user approval. Target: alphaninemarketing.com on Railway via `npm run serve` / `server.js`.

## Build & deploy

- `npm run build` = CRA build + `scripts/apply-cache-headers.js` + `scripts/inject-asset-preloads.js`
- Production: `server.js` (Express + compression + long-cache `/static/**`)
- Do not remove post-build scripts from `package.json` `build` script

## `public/index.html` (critical path)

- **Inline critical CSS** (`#critical-css`): hero, navbar shell, footer, `.home` min-height (`220vh` / `280vh` ≤820px), brand-mark, logo dimensions
- **Static LCP shell** inside `#root` (`#lcp-shell`): must mirror `.app` grid children in order:
  1. `<header class="navbar navbar--home">` (logo `logo-nav.webp`, 40×40)
  2. `<main>` → `.home` → hero eyebrow + `#hero-heading`
  3. `<footer class="footer">` (same tagline text, `logo-footer.webp` 56×72, brand-mark)
- Preloads: `logo-nav.webp` (high), `logo-footer.webp`
- Fonts: load via `requestIdleCallback` + `media="print"` onload; `display=optional`; `fonts-loading` class on `<html>`

## Post-build (`scripts/inject-asset-preloads.js`)

- Convert blocking `main.*.css` to non-blocking: `media="print" onload="this.media='all'"` + `<noscript>` fallback
- Preload only `main.*.js` with `fetchpriority="high"` (dedupe paths with leading `/`)
- Do not re-add CSS preload that blocks render

## React routing & bundles

- **`Home` is eager** in `App.js` (LCP hero); other pages stay `lazy()`
- Hero **`h1` + eyebrow are plain HTML** (not `m.*`); motion only on below-fold hero blocks
- `LazyMotion` + `domAnimation` via `MotionProvider`; defer `HeroScene`, `CursorGlow`
- Below-fold home sections: `DeferredSection` + lazy `HomeServicesSection` / `HomePortfolioSection` / `HomeTeamSection`

## CLS guards

- `.app` uses `grid-template-rows: auto 1fr auto` — static shell **must** include navbar + main + footer (never main-only)
- `.home { min-height: 220vh }` (280vh mobile) prevents footer jump when chunks load
- `.footer { min-height: 22rem }` (42rem ≤767px); `.footer__tagline { min-height: 2.88em }`; `.brand-mark { min-height: 2.75rem }`
- Footer logo: `PUBLIC_URL/logo-footer.webp`, explicit `width`/`height`, no `loading="lazy"`

## Images & LCP

- Nav/footer logos: transparent WebP in `public/` (`logo-nav.webp`, `logo-footer.webp`); regenerate via `npm run optimize-logos` from `logo.png` / `logo2.png` (trim + alpha, no black box)
- Portfolio videos: mobile tap-to-play; no in-view autoplay on mobile lite
- Use `useMobileLite` / `mobile-performance.css` for reduced motion/blur on mobile

## When adding features

- New above-fold UI: extend critical CSS + static shell if it affects first paint
- New global CSS: stays in main bundle; do not make `main.css` render-blocking again
- New routes: keep code-split; do not lazy-load Home
- Test with Lighthouse mobile after deploy before claiming perf is unchanged
